<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 13-AUG.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 13-AUG.</headline>
<text>
<p>Supertyphoon Winnie is now moving away from the Mariana Islands. The storm hit the central and northern islands with damage winds, flooding rains, and heavy coastal storm surge. Major damage is likely and will be assessed over the next few days. Winnie has 160 mph winds and will move west northwestward away from the islands over open water during the next 24 hours as a major threat to shipping.  </p>
<p>Nothing further at this time.</p>
</text>
